# PROVENANCE: data/derived/md_surrogate_bedroc.csv

**Producer:** hand-run — no automated reproducer in `reproduce/`.

**How it was made.** Exported by an ad-hoc cell in an earlier version of what is now
`notebooks/22_bedroc_baselines.ipynb` (was NB 10 in the pre-flatten numbering).
The cell built the joined table `MD features × metadata × GBSA @ locked combo`,
computed BEDROC α=20 per target for three scorers (docking / GBSA_locked / MD_surrogate)
and wrote the per-target values out. The current NB 22 code recomputes the same numbers
inline but no longer persists them to disk — the CSV is a historical snapshot.

**Columns:** `target, n_labeled, n_gbsa, docking, GBSA_locked, MD_surrogate, MD+lig_surrogate`.

**Consumers.** No live consumer script or notebook reads this file. It is referenced
by `notebooks/00_data_catalog.ipynb` (section 3) as a legacy artifact and by
`docs/DATA_LINEAGE.md` for provenance.

**Status.** Orphan / snapshot. Do NOT rely on it for new analyses — use
`data/derived/canonical_baselines.csv` (produced by `reproduce/canonical_baselines.py`)
for the authoritative panel BEDROC values, and rerun NB 22 to regenerate per-target
values in memory.

**To regenerate on demand.** Open `notebooks/22_bedroc_baselines.ipynb`, run through
the "Connect to BEDROC" and "Per-target BEDROC" cells, then export the
`bedroc_pivot` DataFrame with `bedroc_pivot.to_csv(DERIVED / 'md_surrogate_bedroc.csv')`.
